    <notes>
        This profile uses the REST API via a relay server running on localhost:5000.
        The relay server is completely stateless - it authenticates with Barco per-request
        and does not store session state.

        All control actions send api_key and barco_ip directly to the relay server,
        which handles authentication and relays the command. This eliminates the need
        for Savant to manage session cookies or refresh them.

        Controls Power On/Off, Input Selection, Brightness, and Preset/Profile Selection.
        Inputs use HDMI and DisplayPort.

        USAGE:
        1. Set Barco_IP state variable to your Barco Video Wall Manager IP
        2. Set API_Key state variable to your Barco API key (from VwM UI Security page)
        3. Call control actions directly (PowerOn, SetBrightness, etc.)
           Each action automatically authenticates with Barco and executes the command

    </notes>

    <control_interfaces preferred="ip" control_optional="false">
        <ip port="5000" response_time_length_ms="6000" protocol="tcp">
            <send_postfix type="hex">0D0A</send_postfix>
            <receive_end_condition test_condition="data" type="hex">0D0A</receive_end_condition>
        </ip>
    </control_interfaces>

